I stand in front of the counter.
'How much is the total?' I ask.
The person at the counter looks at me and smiles.
'Two hundred and fifty rupees,' he says.
I take money from my bag.
I give him two hundred and fifty rupees.
He gives me the bill.
'The iced tea is very tasty,' I say.
'Thank you very much.'
'Thank you.'
'Please come again,' he says happily.
I open the glass door of the café.
I step outside.
Outside, it is still very sunny.
I feel the March heat again.
But now I feel very refreshed.
I walk forward along the road.
